00:20:01,720 --> 00:20:02,460
Oh, man.

257
00:20:03,160 --> 00:20:07,120
Unfortunately, there can be a lot of drama associated with scouting,

258
00:20:07,860 --> 00:20:11,820
and a lot of it seems to center around the process of becoming an Eagle Scout.

259
00:20:11,940 --> 00:20:16,260
And I'm going to share with you my experience and what I know.

260
00:20:16,420 --> 00:20:17,580
I do not know everything.

261
00:20:17,820 --> 00:20:18,980
I have not seen it all.

262
00:20:19,480 --> 00:20:22,240
But I will tell you, I've worked with about, in round numbers,

263
00:20:22,660 --> 00:20:25,780
somewhere between 50 and 60 scouts who've earned the rank of Eagle.

264
00:20:25,780 --> 00:20:30,320
And becoming an Eagle is beset by difficulties, and it should be.

265
00:20:30,440 --> 00:20:31,720
It's supposed to be challenging.

266
00:20:32,520 --> 00:20:37,780
Unfortunately, the normal difficulties are often compounded by totally unnecessary complications,

267
00:20:38,620 --> 00:20:41,160
and I call those complications drama.

268
00:20:42,340 --> 00:20:48,080
All too often, it's the Scoutmaster that ends up causing the drama.

269
00:20:48,899 --> 00:20:50,399
Yeah, I have.

270
00:20:50,899 --> 00:20:51,540
I have.

271
00:20:51,540 --> 00:20:56,280
I'm guilty as anybody, but I have picked up a few things along the way.

272
00:20:56,379 --> 00:21:01,639
I mean, somehow, there are a number of Scoutmasters who act like they are the gatekeepers for advancement,

273
00:21:02,720 --> 00:21:05,159
especially when it comes to the rank of Eagle.

274
00:21:06,740 --> 00:21:10,659
And really, they're supposed to be coaches and guides and mentors.

275
00:21:11,139 --> 00:21:15,540
Some Scoutmasters develop the idea that their personal standard of achievement is all important.

276
00:21:15,540 --> 00:21:21,000
They wield the Scoutmasters conference and signatures on documents like a weapon,

277
00:21:21,780 --> 00:21:25,879
making it a pronouncement of their often capricious judgment.

278
00:21:27,020 --> 00:21:29,760
This all sounds pretty dramatic because it really is dramatic.

279
00:21:30,200 --> 00:21:38,820
I mean, Scouts and families take a huge emotional hit when the shockwaves extend past the Scoutmasters' actions into their home.

280
00:21:39,899 --> 00:21:43,080
Narratives of these dramas unfold as if they'd been scripted.

281
00:21:43,080 --> 00:21:45,679
And I'll tell you, I get emails about this all the time.

282
00:21:45,800 --> 00:21:46,600
I read about it.

283
00:21:47,040 --> 00:21:49,220
I have people talk to me about it.

284
00:21:50,220 --> 00:21:52,100
Here's the way it usually works.

285
00:21:52,340 --> 00:21:58,340
You know, a Scout has completed their Eagle project, their six months of leadership tenure, their 21 merit badges.

286
00:21:59,040 --> 00:22:01,540
They've had six previous Scoutmaster conferences.

287
00:22:01,540 --> 00:22:08,440
And they sit down with the Scoutmaster and he ambushes them with one or two pronouncements.

288
00:22:10,240 --> 00:22:16,740
It can be that he's not met the active requirement or that he has failed to show Scout spirit.

289
00:22:17,440 --> 00:22:23,100
Sometimes the Scoutmaster may set the Scout a task to appease him.

290
00:22:23,100 --> 00:22:29,439
And sometimes the Scoutmaster just slams the gate closed and says, you're never going to become an Eagle Scout.

291
00:22:30,080 --> 00:22:31,480
I mean, can you believe that this happens?

292
00:22:31,540 --> 00:22:31,919
It does.

293
00:22:32,080 --> 00:22:33,840
It happens more than you would think.

294
00:22:35,080 --> 00:22:37,060
And why does it happen over and over again?

295
00:22:38,260 --> 00:22:44,580
Usually because the Scoutmaster either lacks an understanding of the advancement system or he is just generally frustrated.

296
00:22:45,139 --> 00:22:47,439
Now, what do I mean by just generally frustrated?

297
00:22:47,440 --> 00:22:51,120
The best explanation I have is drawn from my personal experience.

298
00:22:51,920 --> 00:22:58,060
Most of us develop an internalized, idealized concept of what an Eagle Scout should be.

299
00:22:58,680 --> 00:23:01,380
And it becomes a standard by which we judge Scouts.

300
00:23:02,160 --> 00:23:09,680
And this idealized personal standard supplants the advancement process and results in a whole lot of frustration.

301
00:23:09,680 --> 00:23:20,300
I got to tell you, it took me a lot of years to understand that no Scout was going to measure up to the idealized standard of perfection that I had developed for myself.

302
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:22,040
I'm not perfect.

303
00:23:22,720 --> 00:23:24,680
I couldn't measure up to that standard.

304
00:23:25,060 --> 00:23:29,580
But I had in my mind that an Eagle Scout should be this way.

305
00:23:30,120 --> 00:23:31,840
And that was the way it was going to be.

306
00:23:32,500 --> 00:23:37,440
And upholding that standard was doing a lot more harm than it was good.

307
00:23:37,440 --> 00:23:46,340
The antidote to this dilemma was an understanding of what Scouting is really about and what makes it different from any other field of endeavor.

